From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: husky-port CI <ci@husky-port.local>
Date: Tue, 4 Nov 2026 12:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gki_defconfig: default to LTO_NONE (zuma thin-LTO CFI
 mis-link)

olddefconfig resolves the LTO choice to its default (CLANG_THIN) after
fragment merging on this kleaf version, defeating fragment-set LTO_NONE.
Set it in the base defconfig so no merge order can re-assert THIN.
Matches LOS kernel (LTO_NONE).

---
 arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
index 052f7835d9c6..b62e8a994f22 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
@@ -774,3 +774,7 @@
 CONFIG_KUNIT_DEBUGFS=y
 # CONFIG_KUNIT_DEFAULT_ENABLED is not set
 # CONFIG_RUNTIME_TESTING_MENU is not set
+CONFIG_LTO_NONE=y
+# CONFIG_LTO_CLANG_THIN is not set
+# CONFIG_LTO_CLANG_FULL is not set
+# CONFIG_LTO_CLANG is not set
